$\begin{align}
\blueE{50\%} \text{ of }\maroonD{950} &= \blueE{\dfrac{50}{100}} \cdot \maroonD{950}\\\\
&=\blueE{\dfrac{1}{2}} \cdot \maroonD{950}
\end{align}$

$\blueE{50\%}$ of a number *always* equals $\blueE{\dfrac{1}{2}}$ of the number.

What is $\blueE{\dfrac{1}{2}}$ of $\maroonD{950}$?
